    "\n",
    "The second group is dominated by adult to elderly women who are widowed, around 41 years old, and have a middle-level income. Unlike the first group, the total purchases made by this group rank as the second highest among all groups, amounting to $370.50. Why is the total spending in this group significantly different from the first group, even though their age range is not very different? Gender becomes one of the influencing factors. This is evident from the top product categories purchased: Jewelry & Accessories, followed by personal care (health) items, which makes sense given that this group is dominated by women.\n",
    "\n",
    "Customers in this group make purchases approximately 5 times per month, although the brands they choose tend to vary (they do not stick to a single brand), as shown by their low loyalty rate of only 40.6%. Customers in this group also seem less interested in membership programs, with only 80 people owning a membership card.\n",
    "\n",
    "Their reasons for purchasing products are primarily driven by needs associated with women’s daily necessities. Customers in this group tend to prefer online platforms for their shopping activities."
   ]
