   "source": [
    "## B. Business Recommendation"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "### Cluster 0  Business Recommendations – (Male, 42 Years Old, High Income, In-Store Shopper, Impulsive Buyer)"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "1. Create In-Store Experiences That Trigger Impulsive Purchases\n",
    "Since customers in this cluster tend to make impulsive purchases directly in-store, leverage attractive point-of-sale merchandising such as placing Animal Feed, Arts & Crafts products, and hotel vouchers near the checkout area or along main store pathways. Add limited-time offers and small bundle deals to encourage spontaneous decisions. Strong visual cues and on-the-spot promotions will further reinforce their impulsive buying behavior.\n",
    "\n",
    "2. Premium Loyalty Perks for Brand-Loyal Customers\n",
    "With relatively high brand loyalty (65%) and many already holding membership cards, offer exclusive perks such as members-only early access, special discounts for the second purchase within the same month, or complimentary services (e.g., free pet-food delivery for Animal Feed purchases). This strategy boosts customer retention and increases the basket size per visit.\n",
    "\n",
    "3. Special Packages & Promotions for High-Income Segments\n",
    "Although these customers have high income, their spending per transaction tends to be low. Therefore, direct promotions toward premium and experience-based products (e.g., hotel vouchers, exclusive art workshops). Use refined cross-selling strategies—such as bundling premium Animal Feed with coupons for pet-friendly hotels—to increase purchase value in a way that aligns with their lifestyle. This can raise the average purchase amount without requiring customers to shop more frequently."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "###  Cluster 1 Business Recommendations – (Female, 41 Years Old, Middle Income, Online Shopper, Need-Based Buyer)"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "1. Personalized Product Bundling Tailored to Women’s Needs\n",
    "Focus your offers on categories such as Jewelry & Accessories, Health Care, and Toys & Games by creating bundles that fit the everyday needs of women in their 40s. For example, a “Self-Care & Family” bundle combining simple jewelry, health products, and toys for children or grandchildren. This type of personalization increases product relevance and encourages more frequent purchases, even though brand loyalty in this cluster is low.\n",
    "\n",
    "2. Optimize a Premium yet Simple Online Shopping Experience\n",
    "Since most purchases occur online, ensure that the shopping platform features easy navigation, high-quality product images, and a one-click purchase option to simplify checkout. Considering the average age of customers, a clean and intuitive UI/UX reduces friction during the buying process. Include friendly customer support via chat or WhatsApp to assist during shopping.\n",
    "\n",
    "3. Thematic Discounts & Event-Based Exclusive Membership Options\n",
    "Boost customer interest in loyalty programs by offering versions that do not require long-term commitment. For example, an event-based loyalty scheme like “Shop 3 times this month and get 15% off on Health Care products.” This approach aligns with their need-based purchasing behavior while providing relevant incentives. It also encourages initial engagement that can grow into long-term loyalty."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "### Cluster 2 Business Recommendations – (Male, 37 Years Old, High Income, Mixed Channel Shopper, Wants-Based Buyer)"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "1. Exclusivity & Premium Membership to Leverage High Brand Loyalty\n",
    "Since this cluster has exceptionally high brand loyalty (90%) but relatively low membership participation, introduce a premium membership program offering exclusive benefits such as early access to product launches, extended warranties for Home Appliances, and invitations to members-only sports events. Targeting this segment with a program that differentiates them from regular shoppers will maximize long-term retention potential.\n",
    "\n",
    "2. “Lifestyle Upgrade” Campaigns to Trigger Wants-Based Purchases\n",
    "Customers in this cluster buy based on desire rather than necessity. Leverage marketing storytelling that emphasizes lifestyle aspirations—for example, promoting Home Appliances with smart-home concepts or pairing Sports & Outdoors products with premium adventure themes. Use thematic promotions that evoke emotion and aspiration, rather than relying solely on price discounts.\n",
    "\n",
    "3. Strengthen Omnichannel Strategy for a Seamless Journey\n",
    "Because customers use both online and offline channels, create a consistent and interconnected experience. Examples include: buy online & pick up in-store (click & collect), or checking offline stock availability through the app. Offer extra coupons or loyalty points when customers complete purchases across different channels. This approach enhances convenience while reinforcing brand engagement at every touchpoint."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "### Cluster 3 Business Recommendations – (Female, 27 Years Old, High Income, Mixed Channel Shopper, Need-Based Buyer)"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "1. Need-Based Product Bundling Strategies\n",
    "Since customers in this cluster make purchases driven by practical needs, the business can offer product bundles that combine Sports & Outdoors, Jewelry & Accessories, and Gardening & Outdoors categories. For example, a “Healthy Active Lifestyle” bundle that includes sports equipment, sporty fashion accessories, and gardening tools to support a balanced, health-oriented lifestyle. This strategy encourages higher-value purchases while helping customers fulfill multiple needs in a single transaction.\n",
    "\n",
    "2. Personalized Omnichannel Shopping Experience\n",
    "With mixed purchasing channels (online & offline), customers benefit greatly when businesses integrate purchasing data from both channels to provide personalized product recommendations. For instance, the system could recommend accessories or gardening tools after a customer buys sports equipment. This interconnected experience strengthens loyalty and maximizes customer retention.\n",
    "\n",
    "3. Lifestyle-Driven Loyalty Program\n",
    "The high loyalty rate (81%) can be further enhanced through a lifestyle-based loyalty program—offering bonus points for purchases in categories tied to healthy and active living. Examples include double points for Sports & Outdoors purchases during sports seasons, or special rewards for customers who frequently buy across two different categories. This approach keeps the loyalty program relevant to the customer's lifestyle and needs."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "### Cluster 4 Business Recommendations – (Female, 30 Years Old, High Income, In-Store Shopper, Need-Based Buyer)"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "1️. Premium Loyalty Program with High-Value Incentives\n",
    "With brand loyalty still low (43%) and only 41.5% of customers registered as members, the business should launch a premium loyalty program that offers immediate, high-value benefits. Examples include special discounts for purchases above a certain amount, exclusive in-store events, or priority service for popular categories such as Packages and Mobile Accessories. The goal is to convert these frequent shoppers into loyal, long-term customers.\n",
    "\n",
    "2️. Bundled Offers for Daily Needs and Lifestyle Purchases\n",
    "Since customer purchases are largely need-driven, bundling packages that combine Food & Beverages with Mobile Accessories or additional services (e.g., a meal package + gadget care kit) can attract interest while increasing the average transaction value. This strategy is particularly relevant for customers with busy lifestyles who appreciate convenience when shopping in-store.\n",
    "\n",
    "3️. Personalized In-Store Shopping Experience Through Technology\n",
    "The dominance of the in-store channel presents an opportunity to deliver data-driven personalization. The business can leverage in-store CRM or digital kiosks to display product recommendations based on customers’ purchase history. With a high purchase frequency (10 times per month), personalized experiences will enhance relevance, strengthen customer relationships, and drive repeat purchases in key categories.\n",
    "\n",
    "If you'd like, I can also refine this for a presentation deck or make it more concise."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "### Cluster 5 Business Recommendations – (Woman, 27 Years Old, Middle Income, Online, Impulsive)"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "1️. Flash Sales and Limited-Time Offers to Maximize Impulsive Purchases\n",
    "\n",
    "Since customers tend to shop impulsively, urgency-based promotions such as flash sales, limited-time offers, or countdown deals can encourage more frequent purchases. Focus these promotions on key categories such as Health Supplements and Gardening & Outdoors to increase relevance and maximize spontaneous purchase responses.\n",
    "\n",
    "2️. Membership Gamification to Boost Loyalty\n",
    "\n",
    "Although brand loyalty is low, membership participation is relatively high (56.8%). This can be leveraged by adding gamification elements such as bonus points for consecutive purchases, weekly shopping challenges, or exclusive online challenges. The goal is to turn membership into an active engagement channel that keeps customers coming back and choosing the same brand.\n",
    "\n",
    "3️. Personalized Product Recommendations Based on Online Activity\n",
    "\n",
    "With online shopping as the dominant channel, using an AI-driven recommendation engine that learns impulsive shopping patterns can help display relevant products on the homepage or at checkout. For example, after purchasing Health Supplements, the system can offer Furniture for home wellness or Gardening tools as add-ons. This strategy can increase basket size without requiring a significant increase in spending per visit."
   ]
