    "# VII. Conclusion"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "This project aims to optimize the understanding of the customer base through a data-driven customer segmentation approach. The process begins with data preprocessing to ensure data quality, including cleaning, standardizing numerical variables, and encoding categorical variables.\n",
    "\n",
    "The K-Means Clustering method is then applied to group customers based on their shopping behavior patterns and demographic characteristics. Through model performance evaluation, six clusters were identified as the most optimal segmentation structure. Each cluster is analyzed in depth to identify customer profiles, purchase motivations, loyalty levels, and preferred transaction channels.\n",
    "\n",
    "The results of this analysis are translated into actionable business insights and personalized marketing strategies for each segment. This approach provides a strategic foundation for the company to improve targeting accuracy, strengthen customer loyalty, and maximize long-term customer value."
   ]
